{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-178662",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that if $a\\ge 0,$ then\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{a}^{2}}=a.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that $4$ and $25$ are both perfect squares, where\n\n$$\n4={2}^{2},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n25={5}^{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, to work out $\\sqrt{\\frac{4}{25}},$ we express $\\frac{4}{25}$ as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\frac{4}{25}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{\\frac{{2}^{2}}{{5}^{2}}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{\\frac{2\\cdot 2}{5\\cdot 5}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{(\\frac{2}{5})}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
